-- PARANOIA FRAMEWORK MANDATE: EVERY SINGLE FOREIGN KEY MUST HAVE A CORRESPONDING INDEX. FAILURE TO ADD AN INDEX TO A CASCADING KEY WILL CAUSE PRODUCTION OUTAGES DURING DELETIONS.
-- GDPR MANDATE: EVERY TABLE STORING PII (leads, messages, linkedin data, ai responses) MUST reference workspace_id with ON DELETE CASCADE. Failure to do so violates GDPR Article 17.
-- =================================================================
-- CANONICAL SCHEMA — ELE-IN
-- Last synced with: 016_settings_production.sql
-- DO NOT EDIT this file manually to fix live DB issues.
-- Run migrations instead. This file is for fresh-install only.
-- =================================================================

-- ==============================================================================
-- ELE-IN · SUPABASE PRODUCTION SCHEMA v3 (PostgreSQL 15+)
-- ==============================================================================
-- v2 fixed: #1-#12 + bonus tables.
-- v3 fixes (second audit pass):
--   A. Cookie mechanism unified — BYTEA blob = envelope-encrypted ciphertext;
--   B. RLS WITH CHECK on join-traversal policies (list_members, lead_states,
--   C. accounts (workspace_id, status) index added (plain + partial variants).
--   D. outbox_events.idempotency_key UNIQUE — prevents double-fire on retry.
--   E. accounts.is_active converted to GENERATED ALWAYS from (status = 'ACTIVE').
--   F. sanitize_template_on_publish() trigger strips account refs before publish.
--   G. lead_states.attempts + max_attempts — exponential backoff tracking.
-- Idempotent: safe to re-run.
-- ==============================================================================

